      ],
      "source": "https://www.lompicopark.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1915 logging era left the Roaring Camp Railroad, now a tourist line that runs from Felton through the Henry Cowell Redwood Forest to Santa Cruz.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lompicopark.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lompico’s early 20th‑century community hosted a brass band and nightly concerts in Lompico Park during the 1920s‑1940s.",
